# Design system (blueprint)

Stream Kit marketing and dashboard UIs share a **blueprint** visual language inspired by Cloudflare product pages: persistent vertical rails, full-bleed hairline rules, crosshair intersections, and collapsed-border schematic grids.

Use `@stream-kit/ui/blueprint` primitives — do not reinvent rails, crosshairs, or cell grids with one-off markup.

## Primitives

| Import from `@stream-kit/ui/blueprint` | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `GridFrame` | Page shell with content column + vertical rails + hatched gutters |
| `SectionRule` | Full-width horizontal hairline between sections (optional crosshairs) |
| `Crosshair` | `+` markers at rail/rule intersections and panel corners |
| `CellGrid` / `Cell` | Collapsed-border schematic grids (shared borders, no card gaps) |
| `Panel` | Sharp-cornered bordered surface; optional header rule + corner crosshairs. Tone: `default` (marketing), `solid` (app cards), `flush` (nested) |
| `Eyebrow` | Mono uppercase label with optional index (`01 / FEATURES`) |

Utilities (from `packages/ui/src/styles/blueprint.css`, imported via app/site `layout.css`):

- `blueprint-grid` — masked 48px background grid
- `blueprint-hatch` — diagonal hatch for gutters / CTA bands
- `blueprint-ticks` — ruler tick marks along a rule
- `blueprint-rule-x` / `blueprint-rule-y` — full-bleed escape rules

## Radius (hybrid)

- **Structural surfaces** (`Panel`, cell grids, data-table, empty-state, floating menus, alerts, nav items): `rounded-none`.
- **Controls** (buttons, inputs, badges): keep a small radius (`rounded-lg` / `rounded-md`). The theme `--radius-xl` is tightened so leftover `rounded-xl` classes still read sharp.
- Do not reintroduce `rounded-xl border border-dark-600 bg-dark-800` floating cards — use `Panel tone="solid"`.

## Rules

1. **Rails once** — draw vertical rails via a single `GridFrame` in the marketing layout, never per section. App shell uses a left-nav rail instead.
2. **Hairlines vs UI borders** — schematic lines use `border-rule` / `bg-rule` / `text-rule-strong`. Interactive UI chrome (inputs, buttons, dialogs) keeps `border-border`. Floating menus keep `border-dark-600` for readable edges above content.
3. **Sharp structure** — structural frames use `rounded-none`. Radius stays on controls.
4. **Collapsed grids over gapped cards** — prefer `CellGrid` + `Cell` over `gap-4` floating cards for feature matrices and marketplace grids. Exception: drag-and-drop dashboard grids stay gapped.
5. **Eyebrow anatomy** — section intros: `Eyebrow` (optional index) → `h2` in `font-outfit` → muted lede → content.
6. **No decorative gradients** outside ambient backgrounds (`blueprint-grid`, `boot-ambient`). Do not add purple/blue glow blobs on marketing sections.
7. **Prefer tokens** — never hardcode hex/oklch for rules; use `--color-rule` / `--color-rule-strong`.

## Anti-patterns

```svelte
<!-- ❌ Floating rounded cards with strong borders for marketing grids -->
<article class="rounded-xl border border-dark-600 bg-dark-800 p-6">…</article>

<!-- ✅ Schematic cell -->
<Cell>
  <p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-primary">01</p>
  …
</Cell>
```

```svelte
<!-- ❌ Per-section vertical lines -->
<section class="border-x border-dark-600">…

<!-- ✅ One GridFrame in the layout -->
<GridFrame>…</GridFrame>
```
